\section{Hardware Specifications and BOM}
\subsection{Primary Processing Unit}
The CLE accelerator card is built on a PCIe Gen 5 platform featuring:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Dual-die FPGA logic fabrics (UltraScale+/Agilex-class).
    \item HBM3e memory stacks providing $>1~\text{TB/s}$ bandwidth.
    \item Integrated ML-KEM-1024 NTT cryptographic block.
    \item FP64 multi-precision vector units for scientific kernels.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Thermal Sink Interface}
Thermal management is achieved through:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Loop-Heat-Pipe (LHP) chassis with capillary-driven phase transport.
    \item Graphite-composite vapor chamber for hotspot suppression.
    \item Radiative fins for vacuum-compatible dissipation.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Interconnect Standard}
CLE nodes communicate via:
\begin{itemize}
    \item CXL 2.0 coherent memory fabric.
    \item Zero-copy telemetry ingestion windows.
    \item Deterministic accelerator handshakes.
\end{itemize}

\section{Implementation Workflow and Deployment Blueprint}
\subsection{Phase I: Physical Layout and Schematics}
Netlists are imported into Altium or Cadence environments with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Single-ended impedance: $50~\Omega \pm 5\%$.
    \item Differential impedance: $100~\Omega \pm 5\%$.
    \item EMI suppression via stitching vias every $2$--$3~\text{mm}$.
    \item VRM ripple maintained below $10~\text{mV}$.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Phase II: Firmware and Logic Synthesis}
SystemVerilog netlists are compiled into FPGA bitstreams with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Zero timing violations across all clock domains.
    \item Full static timing analysis (STA).
    \item Verified clock-domain crossing (CDC) boundaries.
    \item Constant-time ML-KEM-1024 NTT execution under jitter injection.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Phase III: System Integration}
A C++20 host control wrapper manages:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Real-time telemetry ingestion via CXL windows.
    \item Accelerator handshake protocol:
    \[
        \text{init} \rightarrow \text{ready} \rightarrow \text{dispatch} 
        \rightarrow \text{compute} \rightarrow \text{sync} \rightarrow \text{commit}.
    \]
    \item Unified logging for hydrodynamic, thermodynamic, cryptographic, and sensor domains.
\end{itemize}

